# These PTX files are CHECKED-IN test fixtures (the OptiX module compiler re-JITs
# them to the device SM at runtime), not build artifacts — override the global
# *.ptx ignore so they stay tracked and regeneration via the sibling .cu is visible.
!optix_progs.ptx
!optix_tri.ptx
# M2 Phase-1 spike: PTX emitted from the hand-authored .ll by the fork's NVPTX llc
# (gen_optix_ll.py -> optix_progs_ll.ll -> llc -> this). Checked in so the LLVM->PTX
# OptiX-acceptance test fixture is reproducible without a fork-llc run.
!optix_progs_ll.ptx
# the .ll is the source of truth (gen_optix_ll.py writes it; llc consumes it);
# override the global *.ll ignore so it stays tracked alongside its PTX.
!optix_progs_ll.ll
# the standalone spike harness builds to an exe — never track it
spike_optix_ll.exe
